  "method": "Key Largo reef line from Carysfort south to Pickles/Snapper Ledge: started from the NOAA FKNMS 2025 mooring-buoy layer and Shipwreck Trail, Monroe County TDC's Reef Explorer guide and the FWC artificial-reef dataset, then checked each candidate against five Key Largo/Tavernier operators' own dive-site pages (Rainbow Reef, BlueWater Divers, Pirates Cove Watersports, Silent World, Sea Dwellers, Conch Republic Divers). Counting rule: named, recreational scuba (not snorkel-only, technical-depth, closed or permit-only), and on at least two independent lists. NOAA FKNMS's mooring-buoy list and its Shipwreck Trail are one publisher and count once; Monroe County TDC's Reef Explorer guide and its shipwrecks page count once; FWC's artificial-reef dataset counts once and only for a named vessel an operator also advertises; each dive operator's own published site list counts once (Captain Hook's and its Dive Key West shop are one operator). Lodging guides, magazines and hobby sites were read but never counted. Counted 2026-10-14.",
